    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **38 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the new `Cp27Tests` (both cases green).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `contactPreference` field so the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response returns `'EMAIL'` when an owner has an email, otherwise `'PHONE'`.\n\nTwo changes, following the existing derived-field pattern (mirroring how `locality`/`membershipLevel` work):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the code generator produces the getter/setter on `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\", expression = \"java(contactPreference(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`, plus a `contactPreference(Owner)` helper that returns `\"EMAIL\"` when the email is present and non-blank, else `\"PHONE\"`.\n\nThe value is derived purely from the owner's own fields at response time, consistent with the other derived fields on the DTO.",
